/T (       Attitudes that support computational thinking:        - Confidence to tackle complex issues.        - Perseverance in the face of difficult problems.        - Dealing with ambiguity and open-ended problems.        - Collaborating and communicating to achieve common goals.        Sub-competencies in computational thinking:        - Formulating problems.        - Organising and analysing data logically.        - Presenting data through abstraction.        - Automating solutions with algorithmic thinking.        - Identifying, analysing and implementing efficient solutions.        - Generalising and applying the solution process to other problems.)
